    "multicolumn_exaVrT": {
      "type": "multicolumn",
      "blocks": {
        "column_TY9WnQ": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/Screenshot_2025-09-05_173200.png",
            "title": "Finally, Smart Glasses That Actually Feel Practical!",
            "text": "<p><br/>I’ve been using the CYAN AI glasses for a couple of weeks now, and they’ve genuinely changed how I move through my day. The ultra-wide 1080p camera is impressive. Photos and videos are crisp, and being able to record hands-free means I catch moments I’d otherwise miss. The open-ear audio is also a big win: calls, podcasts, even music feel immersive, but without totally shutting out the world. The voice command “Hey Cyan” works well for most things, like translating signs, taking quick notes, or pulling up directions.<br/><em><strong>- David Mitchelle</strong></em><br/></p>",
            "link_label": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        "column_w8BEfe": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/Screenshot_2025-09-05_173658.png",
            "title": "Say Cheese! lol",
            "text": "<p>As someone who shoots short video content and is on the go (bike commuting, etc.), the CYAN AI glasses are extremely handy. The five-mic array picks up sound well, even with traffic noise, and switching between the phone and glasses for video is pretty seamless. I like that I can give voice commands “Take a video,” “What’s that sign say?” etc. Without pulling out my phone. The frames are lightweight enough that I forget I’m wearing them after some time.<br/></p><p></p><p><em><strong>-Michael Denver<br/></strong></em></p>",
            "link_label": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        "column_rgqdMg": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/Screenshot_2025-09-19_162855.png",
            "title": "The design is PERFECT!",
            "text": "<p><br/>I was surprised by how modern and subtle these glasses look. They don’t scream “tech” at all, just a clean, stylish pair of frames that fit comfortably all day. I’ve even gotten compliments without people realizing they’re smart glasses, which makes them easy to wear anywhere.<br/></p><p><em><strong>-Kevin Schwartz<br/></strong></em></p>",
            "link_label": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        }
      },
